    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a good start. I'm particularly worried about \"hidden\" risks—the stuff that isn't immediately obvious in the initial paperwork but could cause massive headaches during execution. Could you expand on how we can structure clauses to protect ourselves against bad-faith actors or unexpected \"nuisance\" issues that might arise during the term of the contract?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To counter bad-faith actors, implement rigorous audit rights clauses allowing you to inspect their facilities and processes. Include strong indemnification provisions that hold the supplier responsible for defects, IP infringement, or regulatory breaches. Proactively define what constitutes a material breach and establish clear, escalating remedies before full termination. Finally, include warranties regarding compliance with all relevant German and EU regulations to prevent unexpected legal exposure.",
      "source": "target",
